{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Wehrmacht (] , lit.","title":"Wehrmacht"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" "defence force") was the unified armed forces of Nazi Germany from 1935 to 1946.","title":"Wehrmacht"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It consisted of the "Heer" (army), the "Kriegsmarine" (navy) and the "Luftwaffe" (air force).","title":"Wehrmacht"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The designation "Wehrmacht" for Nazi Germany's military replaced the previously used term, "Reichswehr" (1919–35), and was the manifestation of Nazi Germany's efforts to rearm the nation to a greater extent than the Treaty of Versailles permitted.","title":"Wehrmacht"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"General Friedrich Kühn (7 August 1889 – 15 February 1944) was a General der Panzertruppe in the Wehrmacht during World War II.","title":"Friedrich Kühn"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He was a recipient of the Knight's Cross of the Iron Cross of Nazi Germany.","title":"Friedrich Kühn"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Canadian Armed Forces (CAF; French: "Forces armées canadiennes" , "FAC"), or Canadian Forces (CF) (French: "Forces canadiennes" , "FC"), are the unified armed forces of Canada, as constituted by the National Defence Act, which states: "The Canadian Forces are the armed forces of Her Majesty raised by Canada and consist of one Service called the Canadian Armed Forces."","title":"Canadian Armed Forces"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The XV Mountain Corps was a German military formation that commanded German forces conducting counter-insurgency operations against the Yugoslav Partisans in the Independent State of Croatia during World War II.","title":"XV Mountain Corps (Wehrmacht)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was formed in the Balkans from the staff of the German commander in Croatia (German: "Militärbefehlshabers in Kroatien" ) on 12 August 1943.","title":"XV Mountain Corps (Wehrmacht)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It was subordinated to the 2nd Panzer Army, and from its formation until 1 November 1943 t